+## P57–P62 implementation
+
+### P57 · Native persistence & project recovery diagnostics
+
+`window.CANVIOPersistenceAudit` inspects the existing `CANVIO_81_MEDIA` database and `media` store without requesting a version upgrade. Its explicitly triggered Blob sentinel test verifies add/read/delete against the existing store. If the database does not exist, inspection aborts the implicit create rather than creating a new empty database. Storage estimate and `navigator.storage.persist()` decision are shown separately; a persistence grant is not represented as a backup.
+
+### P58 · Exported media acceptance
+
+`window.CANVIOExportAcceptance.inspectFile(file)` checks a user-selected MP4/WebM file's MIME/extension, size, duration, dimensions and browser `canplay` readiness through a temporary object URL. The file is not uploaded or saved into project storage. This is a decode-readiness check, not proof of audio/video synchronization, complete file integrity or cross-browser export compatibility.
 
-## P56 · Portable ZIP structure preflight & restore preview
+### P59 · Whisper safeguards
 
-`window.CANVIOArchivePreflight.inspect(file)` checks the End of Central Directory, single-disk layout, entry count and directory bounds, entry names, duplicate paths, stored-only compression, flags, local-header/central-directory agreement, offsets, overlaps and the required `full-backup.json` entry. It is read-only and caps the archive at the existing 512 MiB restore limit, 64 entries, 1 MiB central directory and 1,024-byte names. The existing `readStoreZip()` remains the parser and still checks every entry CRC; `CV11.backupIntegrity.verify()` still verifies the payload SHA-256 before data writes.
+The diagnostic fetches the worker only after an explicit user action and checks its pinned runtime/model provenance; it does not download model weights or run inference. The worker validates ArrayBuffer input, non-empty samples, an eight-minute maximum at 16 kHz, supported language values and response shape. Real Vietnamese/English inference, cancellation during real model downloads/inference and memory reclamation remain open acceptance work.
 
-Before the user confirms restore, CANVIO displays a compact inventory: backup date, accepted CANVIO localStorage keys, IndexedDB databases/stores/records, excluded-secret count, source-warning count, checksum state and ZIP entry/size evidence. It does not display secret values or enumerate media payload contents. Cancel leaves project storage unchanged.
+### P60 · Accessibility screening
 
-The validator intentionally accepts only the stored ZIP shape produced by CANVIO `CVZip.build()`. ZIP64, DEFLATE, encrypted entries, data descriptors, multi-disk archives, ZIP comments, extra fields, path traversal and duplicate entries are rejected. This is not a general-purpose third-party ZIP reader.
+A bounded, read-only DOM triage scans accessible names, image alt text, landmarks, heading structure and dialog names. Findings are capped for display and are not a WCAG conformance result. Keyboard-only operation, screen-reader behavior, focus order, contrast and true 200% browser zoom require manual testing.
 
-## P51–P55 features retained
+### P61 · Hosting & security screening
 
-- **P51:** read-only runtime/media capability diagnostics and storage estimate.
-- **P52:** session-scoped render lifecycle ledger, pagehide cancellation and interrupted-job detection; it does not resume MediaRecorder output.
-- **P53:** ZIP signature and 512 MiB size preflight, backup/restore audit and retained CRC/SHA integrity checks.
-- **P54:** heuristic timeline/canvas/device/heap budget; no automatic media mutation.
-- **P55:** unified read-only release report with six pending manual acceptance gates and `releaseCertified:false`.
+A read-only report checks secure-context state, same-origin worker path, external script references and mixed-content references. Server response headers (CSP, CORS, MIME, cache, HSTS and Referrer-Policy) cannot be verified from the page DOM and must be inspected after deployment. The workflow deploys only a successful push to `main`; pull requests and manual dispatch validate/package but do not deploy.
+
+### P62 · Phase 1 release gate
+
+A unified dashboard/report aggregates implementation flags and six mandatory real-world acceptance gates. It is fail-closed and keeps `releaseCertified:false`; this candidate has no self-certification route.
 
